      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lewistown was once a Shawnee reservation before the 1829 Treaty of Lewistown moved the tribes westward.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewistown%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Captain John Lewis, a Shawnee leader who guided the early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewistown%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ohio’s only Revolutionary War fort, Fort Laurens, stands in Lewistown, a relic of frontier defense.",
